## Core Technologies
- Next.js App Router
- TypeScript
- Farcaster Frame v2
- Neynar API Integration
- TailwindCSS for styling

## Code Style and Structure
- Write clean, maintainable TypeScript code
- Use functional components and hooks
- Follow modular architecture patterns
- Use descriptive variable names (e.g., isLoading, hasChannels)
- Implement proper error handling

## File Organization
- Use lowercase with dashes for directories
- Group related components and utilities
- Separate API logic from UI components
- Keep frame-specific logic isolated

## TypeScript Usage
- Use TypeScript for all code files
- Define interfaces for API responses
- Implement proper type safety
- Use zod for API validation

## Component Guidelines
- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- Implement proper loading states
- Use error boundaries where appropriate
- Follow React best practices

## Frame-Specific Rules
- Follow Farcaster Frame v2 specs exactly
- Implement proper frame validation
- Handle frame actions efficiently
- Use appropriate frame metadata

## API and Data Handling
- Use server-side data fetching
- Implement proper caching
- Handle rate limits appropriately
- Process data efficiently
- api access for data in this project is located here: https://data.hubs.neynar.com/api/queries/1049/results.json?api_key=PiIHNfmLRf8rEhvFWkqqZHtW95GgSrQse7MPMmix. We do not need an env if we use that.

## Image Processing
- Optimize channel images server-side
- Implement proper fallbacks
- Use Next.js Image optimization
- Handle various image formats

## Performance
- Minimize client-side JavaScript
- Optimize image loading
- Use proper caching strategies
- Implement efficient data fetching

## Error Handling
- Provide clear error messages
- Implement proper fallbacks
- Log errors appropriately
- Handle edge cases gracefully

Follow Farcaster Frame and Next.js documentation for implementation details. 
